#30002
Choose Your Alignment~
@W========================================@n
@C      STEP 2: CHOOSE YOUR ALIGNMENT   @n
@W========================================@n

Pharasma's servants urge you to select your moral outlook.

@W=== COMMANDS ===@n
• @Ysetalign <alignment>@n - Set alignment (good, neutral, or evil)
• @Ysetethos <ethos>@n     - Set ethos (lawful, neutral, or chaotic)

@W=== EXAMPLES ===@n
• @Ysetalign good@n   + @Ysetethos lawful@n  = Lawful Good
• @Ysetalign neutral@n + @Ysetethos neutral@n = True Neutral
• @Ysetalign evil@n    + @Ysetethos chaotic@n = Chaotic Evil

@W=== ALIGNMENT GUIDE ===@n
@WAlignment:@n Your moral compass
  • @YGood@n    - Selfless, protective, compassionate
  • @YNeutral@n - Balanced, pragmatic, self-interested
  • @YEvil@n    - Selfish, cruel, destructive

@WEthos:@n Your approach to rules and society
  • @YLawful@n  - Honorable, trustworthy, follows codes
  • @YNeutral@n - Flexible, independent, situational
  • @YChaotic@n - Freedom-loving, unpredictable, rebellious

@GTip: Your alignment affects what equipment you can use@n
@GTip: Some classes require specific alignments (e.g., Paladins must be Lawful Good)@n

Go @Ynorth@n when ready to continue.
