#30019
Training Your Character~
@W========================================@n
@C    STEP 5: UNDERSTAND YOUR CHARACTER @n
@W========================================@n

Every level you gain provides multiple benefits.

@W=== WHAT YOU GAIN PER LEVEL ===@n
• @YHit Points@n - More health to survive combat
• @YMove Points@n - Stamina for travel and combat
• @YSkill Points@n - Based on class + Intelligence modifier
• @YSpell Slots@n - For spellcasting classes only
• @YClass Abilities@n - Special powers specific to your class

@W=== FEATS ===@n
Feats are special abilities or bonuses:
  • Start with @Y1 feat@n at level 1
  • Gain @Y1 more@n every @Y3 levels@n (levels 3, 6, 9, etc.)
  • Some classes get @Ybonus feats@n from special lists
  • @YEpic feats@n become available at level 21+

Feats are @Ybinary@n - you either have them or you don't.

@W=== SKILLS ===@n
Skills are ranked abilities (0-20+ ranks):
  • Humans get @Y+1 skill point@n per level (and +4 at level 1)
  • Skills can grant @Ynew abilities@n or @Ypassive bonuses@n
  • Some skills are @Yclass skills@n (easier to improve)

@W=== ABILITY SCORE INCREASES ===@n
Every @Y4 levels@n (4, 8, 12, etc.), you can increase any
ability score by 1 point (Strength, Dexterity, etc.).

@GTip: Type 'help feats' or 'help skills' for detailed information@n
@GTip: Epic levels (21+) unlock powerful new abilities@n

Go @Ynorth@n to learn how to gain your first level.
~
